<title>NETHERLANDS: Bangert sees Ahrend shares at Dfl 100.</title>
<headline>Bangert sees Ahrend shares at Dfl 100.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Sept 18 research.</p>
<p>Company-----Sector-------------price---Broker---------------</p>
<p>    Ahrend	Office furnishing  81.50   Bangert Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Buy (reiterated) - Price target of 100 guilders. Operating margin improved to 10 percent in 1996 first half, which was more important than lower than expected net profit of Dfl 24.1 million. Turnaround in Germany will mainly impact second half year. Management's own forecast rather cautious. Ahrend has developed into value creating &quot;trading&quot; company from value destroying &quot;production&quot; firm.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	4.43     n/a	11.9    1.55</p>
<p>    1996		   5.65     5.85     14.5    2.00</p>
<p>    1997		   7.20     7.00     11.4    2.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
